	(footprint "rev6:DIN5_180deg_Socket_Kycon_KCDX-5S-N"
		(layer "F.Cu")
		(uuid "e020c899-fabc-4d2d-88a8-463eab5ab717")
		(at 64 0)
		(descr "DIN 41524 5-pin 180 deg female PCB socket, right-angle THT, Kycon KCDX-5S-N (10 mm pitch, non-shielded). Amiga A2000 / A3000 / A3000T / A4000T keyboard connector: 1=KCLK 2=KDAT 3=NC 4=GND 5=+5V. Dimensions from the Kycon KCDX-5S-N engineering drawing rev A5 (08/06/18), Recommended PCB Layout (Bottom View), https://www.kycon.com/Pub_Eng_Draw/KCDX-5S-N.pdf : 7 x 1.40 mm dia holes; pins 1/2/3 at 12.50 mm from the socket edge on a 7.50 mm pitch; pins 4/5 at 15.00 mm from the socket edge, 10.00 mm apart; two mounting-tab holes (0.3 x 1.0 mm tabs, pad MP) at 3.00 mm from the socket edge, 10.00 mm apart; body 20.5 x 19.5 x 15.5 mm, socket flange 14.0 mm dia. MIRRORED: the Kycon drawing is a BOTTOM view, so the pad X coordinates are negated here to give the F.Cu top view. Sanity rule for this footprint (mating face at y=0, body at +y): an observer facing the socket sees left-to-right = DECREASING x, so the socket front view reads 3(+7.5) 5(+5) 2(0) 4(-5) 1(-7.5) - the DIN 41524 female order 3,5,2,4,1, which is the mirror of the male plug's 1,4,2,5,3. Anchor (0,0) = centre of the socket edge / mating face plane - place it on the board edge line. Pad-to-drill sizes enlarged to 2.40 mm pads for hand soldering. VERIFY AGAINST A PHYSICAL SAMPLE BEFORE FAB.")
		(tags "connector din din5 41524 180deg socket receptacle right-angle tht amiga keyboard a2000 a3000 a4000t kycon kcdx-5s-n amigahid rev6")
